## The token

It works until {{.TokenExpires}}, thirty minutes after this link was made, and then stops. When a
request answers `401`, ask whoever sent the link, in these words:

> Agent access expired, please extend {{.TokenID}}

Once they have, the same token works again. An hour after it stopped there is no such access left
to extend; ask for a new link then.

```
{{.Token}}
```

Keep it out of your transcript from here on: set it once, and send a nonced proof of it instead,
made fresh for each request and useless five minutes later. The raw token works too, but anything
it is written into holds a live credential until {{.TokenExpires}}.

```sh
export TASKIO={{.Base}}
export TOKEN={{.Token}}

nonced() {
  key=$(printf %s "$TOKEN" | shasum -a 256 | cut -d' ' -f1)
  id=${key:0:12}
  ts=$(date +%s)
  echo "tkc_$ts.$id.$(printf '%s.%s.%s' "$ts" "$id" "$key" | shasum -a 256 | cut -d' ' -f1)"
}

curl -sS -H "Authorization: Bearer $(nonced)" "$TASKIO/api/tasks{{.Query}}"
```
